NativeAOT: tell the JIT which methods never return

The JIT only learns that a callee never returns while scanning it as an inline candidate,
and a [DoesNotReturn] throw helper is NoInlining, so every value live after such a call
was treated as live across a call and kept in a callee-saved register - two executed
instructions per invocation of the caller on the zkVM, in methods whose hot path makes
no call at all. ILC now reports CORINFO_FLG_DOES_NOT_RETURN (a previously unused method
attribute bit) for methods carrying the attribute, matched on the typical method
definition so generic instantiations qualify, and the importer marks a direct call to
such a method no-return; morph then ends the block in a throw and liveness drops.

